>Townsend</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name><name><surname>Cortina-Borja</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Peckham</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name><name><surname>de</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Lyall</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Tookey</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><article-title>Low rates of mother-to-child transmission of HIV following effective pregnancy interventions in the United Kingdom and Ireland, 2000&#x02013;2006</article-title><source>AIDS</source><year>2008</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>973</fpage><lpage>81</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/QAD.0b013e3282f9b67a</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18453857</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Warszawski</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Tubiana</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Le Chenadec</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Blanche</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Teglas</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Dollfus</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Faye</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Burgard</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Rouzioux</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Mandelbrot</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><article-title>Mother-to-child HIV transmission despite antiretroviral therapy in the ANRS French Perinatal Cohort</article-title><source>AIDS</source><year>2008</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>289</fpage><lpage>99</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/QAD.0b013e3282f3d63c</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18097232</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><collab>European Collaborative Study</collab><article-title>The mot